  - title: I haven't told her
    number: 7
    heartsNeeded: 7
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags:
      - story_priya_6
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I haven't told Mum. About the academy.
    - After Dad's card, she sat in the kitchen for ages. I'm not adding to that. She'd tell me to go. She'd tell me to go and then sit in the kitchen on her own every night.
    - Coach Lucia knows. She said, 'Your mum is tougher than both of us, Dev.' Which is true. But that's not the point.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Stay or go
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I have to tell the academy by Saturday. That's the day after the Suburb Cup draw.
    - If I stay, I play the Cup with the street. Ji-ho, Nia, everybody. Against the city team. And Mum's not alone.
    - If I go, I might actually make it. Proper football. I'd send money home. I'd have a Sterling badge on my shirt, though. Every day.
    - You don't have to be nice about it. Just tell me what you'd do.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Stay with the team
      replyA:
      - Stay. Yeah. I think I needed somebody to say it so I could stop arguing with myself.
      - I'm telling Mum tonight. All of it. And then I'm telling Coach we're going to win the Cup.
      flagsA:
      - dev_stayed
      optionB: Join the academy
      replyB:
      - Go. Okay. Okay. I'm going.
      - I'm telling Mum tonight. She's going to cry and then pack my bag before I've finished talking. I know her.
      flagsB:
      - dev_academy
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: The Cup final
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - We WON. Three-two, against the Sterling shirts. Nia saved a penalty, Ji-ho dived the right way for once, and I scored the winner with my left. My LEFT.
    - Mum was on the touchline. She'd swapped three shifts to be there. She screamed so loud the crow flew off Kenji's bench.
    - The academy scout came over after. He said the offer's still open next year. I said maybe. Maybe means we'll see.
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: The Sterling tracksuit
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 2
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - The academy's amazing. Pitches like carpet. Coaches who know everything. A gym with machines I don't even know the names of.
    - Every Sunday I come home in the Sterling tracksuit. I take it off before I get to the street. I don't really know why.
    - Mum's okay. She says she's okay. Mrs. Delgado brings her soup now. I think that's a good sign and a bad sign.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Thursday pasta
    number: 10
    heartsNeeded: 10
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Thursday pasta night has got out of hand. Mum invited Coach. Coach brought Mateo. Mateo brought Ji-ho. Ji-ho brought Nia, who brought a beetle.
    - Eleven people in our kitchen. I made the sauce with your tomatoes. Everybody said wow. Not twice. Eleven times.
    - Thanks for telling me to stay. Here. Blue slush. It's for people with hope.
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
